# Shell scripts must keep LF: CRLF breaks them both locally under Git Bash
# ($'\r': command not found) and inside heredocs piped to a remote shell.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Python must keep LF too. scripts/ops/patch-vacuum-guard.py matches an exact
# LF-terminated snippet of the server's hermes_state.py; a CRLF checkout makes
# that literal contain \r\n, the match count drops to 0 and the patch aborts.
*.py text eol=lf

# TypeScript and Vue sources must keep LF as well. Several tests assert against
# the source text itself (readFileSync + toContain with LF-terminated literals,
# e.g. tests/client/chat-panel-runtime-probe-permission.test.ts). On a CRLF
# checkout those pass in CI and fail only on Windows, which hides real
# regressions behind noise. The stored blobs are already LF, so pinning this
# changes no repository content.
*.ts text eol=lf
*.vue text eol=lf
